287
00:21:11.570 --> 00:21:13.220
So what must the agency do?

288
00:21:13.220 --> 00:21:16.348
Everything on this slide is
program design guidance,

289
00:21:16.348 --> 00:21:21.183
not a vendor or standards requirement,
condensed from a seventeen-step checklist.

290
00:21:21.183 --> 00:21:24.844
Before AD DNS retires:
choose one naming authority

291
00:21:24.844 --> 00:21:28.419
for each platform and write
down its length limit.

292
00:21:28.419 --> 00:21:33.472
For Windows, default to classic Autopilot
with Entra join and the serial number,

293
00:21:33.472 --> 00:21:38.295
and use device preparation naming only
once device association is in place.

294
00:21:38.295 --> 00:21:41.245
Inventory who registers each record today.

295
00:21:41.245 --> 00:21:43.964
Make the DHCP server the registrant,

296
00:21:43.964 --> 00:21:48.495
and lock each zone so only the
DHCP servers' keys can update it.

297
00:21:48.495 --> 00:21:54.314
Pick DHCID or TXT ownership records
once, turn off address randomization

298
00:21:54.314 --> 00:21:59.083
on agency Wi-Fi, and create
reverse zones for every DHCP scope.

299
00:21:59.083 --> 00:22:02.027
At cutover: deliver
DNS suffixes both ways,

300
00:22:02.027 --> 00:22:07.244
through DHCP options and router
announcements, and through Intune policy.

301
00:22:07.244 --> 00:22:11.438
For Entra-joined Windows, either
turn client registration off or

302
00:22:11.438 --> 00:22:15.708
accept refused attempts, but never
open zones to unsigned updates.

303
00:22:15.708 --> 00:22:18.246
Handle cloud names and servers separately.

304
00:22:18.246 --> 00:22:21.742
After: turn on scavenging
only after a quiet period,

305
00:22:21.742 --> 00:22:24.407
with lease times matched to its timers.

306
00:22:24.407 --> 00:22:28.846
Monitor duplicates, mismatched
records and devices with no record.

307
00:22:28.846 --> 00:22:32.445
Expect no AAAA records
for SLAAC addresses.

308
00:22:32.445 --> 00:22:35.708
And build certificate names from
the registered device name.

309
00:22:35.708 --> 00:22:44.394
Sources: Research brief,
Agency checklist (steps 1–17,

310
00:22:44.394 --> 00:22:56.110
all PROGRAM DESIGN GUIDANCE) and the
facts each step cites: [S1–S6, S10, S12,

311
00:22:56.110 --> 00:23:06.413
S14–S17, S19–S21, S23, S26, S27, S29, S30,
S34–S39, S41, S43–S46, S48–S52, S54];

312
00:23:06.413 --> 00:23:16.311
the Federal Modernization
Workbook's Book 08 Ch04 and Ch10;

313
00:23:16.311 --> 00:23:22.740
Book 12 Ch02; Book 15 Ch07; Book 07 Ch01.

314
00:23:23.490 --> 00:23:28.665
The decisions: which tool names each kind
of device, and how long names may be.

315
00:23:28.665 --> 00:23:31.994
The DHCP server as the
registrant for endpoints,

316
00:23:31.994 --> 00:23:34.990
and exactly which keys
may update each zone.

317
00:23:34.990 --> 00:23:37.465
DHCID or TXT ownership records.

318
00:23:37.465 --> 00:23:41.215
And whether Entra-joined Windows
PCs try to register at all.

319
00:23:41.215 --> 00:23:43.690
The next steps are the
things I couldn't verify.

320
00:23:43.690 --> 00:23:47.464
Which Apple setting Intune's
Mac rename actually sends,

321
00:23:47.464 --> 00:23:49.515
and how Macs handle DHCP names.

322
00:23:49.515 --> 00:23:54.290
Whether an Entra-joined device's
display name follows an Intune rename.

323
00:23:54.290 --> 00:23:59.325
The Federal Modernization Workbook's Book
05's description of device preparation,

324
00:23:59.325 --> 00:24:04.215
and its note on availability in the higher
government clouds, both need a recheck.

325
00:24:04.215 --> 00:24:09.202
And ask any third-party VPN vendor whether
its concentrator registers clients.

326
00:24:09.202 --> 00:24:10.340
Where does this fit?

327
00:24:10.340 --> 00:24:16.365
Book 05, Chapter 04 covers Intune-first
onboarding and the naming convention.

328
00:24:16.365 --> 00:24:20.695
Book 08 covers the AD DNS
departure in Chapter 04,

329
00:24:20.695 --> 00:24:27.190
cloud private DNS in Chapter 07, and
the migration sequence in Chapter 10.

330
00:24:27.190 --> 00:24:31.726
